expedition to Rome. And then the huge fiasco of the revolution and the recapture of Naples, there is definitely a sense, I think, that Sir William has become much too close to the royal family and that he's slightly lost the plot. So he is replaced as ambassador effectively at the beginning of 1800, a new ambassador is sent out to replace him. And when he gets back to England, a big theme will be he doesn't get the pension he expects, and he doesn't get the peerage, expect. And there's a sense in which people like, well, the Hamilton's are useless. I mean, I hear what you're saying, but from Lord Keith's perspective, he would say, I have this subordinate who is behaving like a diva, who does not follow my orders,
