that this is keith kind of cosplaying a critic in antony and cleopatra or something but that doesn't mean there's not an element of truth in it no i don't think he's doing that i think he's doing that i think he's trying to impose his authority, which is obviously what he should be doing, because he's the commander-in-chief. But the problem is that Nelson, you know, Nelson wins victories by disobeying orders. That's also always been what he does. So there's a classic example of this in the early months of 1800, and it relates to the blockade of Malta. So Keith orders Nelson to abandon Palermo and come to Monorca. Nelson predictably ignores this. He sails out, and on the 18th of February, he wins the single most decisive engagement of the entire blockade of Malta, which is the key
这是基思在扮演《安东尼与克利奥帕特拉》中的评论家之类的角色，但这并不意味着其中没有真理的成分。不，我不认为他在那样做，我认为他在试图行使他的权威，这显然是他应该做的，因为他是总司令。但问题是，纳尔逊，你知道，纳尔逊通过违抗命令赢得胜利。那也一直是他所做的事情。所以 1800 年初有一个经典的例子，它与马耳他的封锁有关。基思命令纳尔逊放弃巴勒莫，去梅诺卡岛。纳尔逊不出所料地无视了这一点。他航行出去，在 2 月 18 日，他赢得了整个马耳他封锁中最具决定性的交战，这是英国的关键

